#### 8. Exception Handling in Tests — `addNullSkuManualCatch()` (line 92)

```java
try {
    catalog.add(null, 1);
    fail("should have thrown");
} catch (Exception ex) {
    assertNotNull(ex.getMessage());
}
```

**Risk:** Manual `try/catch` is verbose and error-prone (forgetting `fail()` lets the test silently pass). JUnit 5 provides `assertThrows` for exactly this case.

**Refactor:**

```java
@Test
void addNullSkuThrows() {
    IllegalArgumentException ex = assertThrows(
        IllegalArgumentException.class,
        () -> catalog.add(null, 1));
    assertNotNull(ex.getMessage());
}
```

